I had to take care of this family.

511
00:30:20,988 --> 00:30:22,072
I'm sorry, Mom.

512
00:30:33,417 --> 00:30:34,668
- You should get some rest.
- It's fine.

513
00:30:34,751 --> 00:30:36,253
I'm fine. It's the pills.

514
00:30:38,714 --> 00:30:40,007
Tell everyone lunch in an hour.

515
00:30:44,469 --> 00:30:45,554
Throw this out.

516
00:30:47,431 --> 00:30:48,307
[Polly yelling]

517
00:30:48,432 --> 00:30:50,184
- Let go of me!
- What's going on?

518
00:30:50,267 --> 00:30:52,019
- She insists on going outside by herself.
- [Polly] No!

519
00:30:52,186 --> 00:30:53,854
- [yelling] No!
- [grunts]

520
00:30:53,979 --> 00:30:54,813
- [Thya] What are you doing, Polly?
- [Joseph] Grandma!

521
00:30:54,897 --> 00:30:56,148
I was just trying to help!

522
00:30:56,273 --> 00:30:57,983
Bonnie! Bonnie!

523
00:30:58,066 --> 00:31:00,360
I've got her. She's trying to steal my money.

524
00:31:00,444 --> 00:31:01,361
- [Thya] Polly!
- [Polly] Call the police!

525
00:31:01,445 --> 00:31:02,321
- Susan, we were just trying--
- [Polly] Let go of me.

526
00:31:02,446 --> 00:31:03,238
[Polly] Bonnie!

527
00:31:03,322 --> 00:31:04,990
- [Joseph] Grandma, are you okay?
- [Susan] Calm down.

528
00:31:05,782 --> 00:31:07,910
- [Polly] It's broken.
- Just a sec, Mom.

529
00:31:15,876 --> 00:31:17,044
You thief.

530
00:31:17,878 --> 00:31:19,046
Oh, my God.

531
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,632
- [pull start rattles]
- [Edgar coughing]

532
00:31:23,592 --> 00:31:24,885
[Edgar coughs hoarsely]

533
00:31:25,469 --> 00:31:26,637
Dad?

534
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:27,513
[metallic clank]

535
00:31:29,014 --> 00:31:30,224
[Edgar continues coughing]

536
00:31:30,307 --> 00:31:31,600
[pull start rattling]

537
00:31:32,351 --> 00:31:33,185
[Joseph] Dad.

538
00:31:34,061 --> 00:31:36,480
[unsettling music playing]

539
00:31:36,605 --> 00:31:37,648
[motor whirring powerlessly]

540
00:31:38,482 --> 00:31:39,316
It's out of gas.

541
00:31:39,399 --> 00:31:40,651
[rattling]

542
00:31:40,734 --> 00:31:42,778
[Edgar breathing heavily]

543
00:31:43,946 --> 00:31:45,531
You don't need to worry about the yard.

544
00:31:45,656 --> 00:31:46,782
[Edgar] Someone's gotta do it.

545
00:31:47,741 --> 00:31:49,660
- I will, I just haven't had--
- We leave you this house...

546
00:31:50,536 --> 00:31:52,079
[inhales] ...and you let it rot.

547
00:31:53,747 --> 00:31:54,748
You like living in shit!

548
00:31:56,959 --> 00:31:58,961
[Edgar coughing]

549
00:32:08,095 --> 00:32:10,389
[continues coughing]

550
00:32:22,693 --> 00:32:23,527
[male voice] Dad.

551
00:32:25,863 --> 00:32:28,282
Dad. Help me.

552
00:32:29,074 --> 00:32:31,535
[uneasy music playing]

553
00:32:52,598 --> 00:32:53,682
[ghostly voice 1] <i>We're inside.</i>

554
00:32:54,474 --> 00:32:57,561
[ghostly voices echoing]

555
00:33:00,480 --> 00:33:01,857
- [ghostly voice 2] <i>Let us in, Dad.</i>
- [grunts]

556
00:33:04,276 --> 00:33:05,068
<i>It's okay.</i>

557
00:33:06,028 --> 00:33:07,988
[ghostly voice 2] <i>Don't fight.</i>

558
00:33:08,572 --> 00:33:10,073
[haunting music playing]

559
00:33:10,157 --> 00:33:11,783
<i>Come on, you can do it.</i>

560
00:33:12,326 --> 00:33:13,160
[echoing] <i>Do it.</i>

561
00:33:14,494 --> 00:33:15,787
<i>Do it. Do it.</i>

562
00:33:17,164 --> 00:33:18,040
[distant rattling]

563
00:33:21,418 --> 00:33:22,211
[Alice] Edgar?

564
00:33:25,214 --> 00:33:26,215
Edgar, are you okay?

565
00:33:29,218 --> 00:33:30,802
- [gasps]
- [glasses shattering]

566
00:33:30,886 --> 00:33:32,429
No, no!

567
00:33:33,013 --> 00:33:34,223
[Edgar grunting]

568
00:33:34,348 --> 00:33:35,474
[both gasp]

569
00:33:35,599 --> 00:33:37,434
[Alice breathing heavily]

570
00:33:42,022 --> 00:33:42,814
[Alice gasps]

571
00:33:47,361 --> 00:33:48,612
Don't tell my wife.

572
00:33:49,488 --> 00:33:51,156
- Please.
- [breathing heavily]

573
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:52,658
I'll hold onto this, okay?

574
00:33:53,617 --> 00:33:54,409
[Edgar] Mmm.

575
00:34:05,212 --> 00:34:06,255
[timer ratcheting]

576
00:34:13,387 --> 00:34:14,388
[door creaks]

577
00:34:17,975 --> 00:34:18,976
- What happened?
- [Alice] Uh...

578
00:34:19,101 --> 00:34:22,396
I missed a step in the cellar.
I dropped the plates. I'm sorry.

579
00:34:22,521 --> 00:34:23,813
[Susan] Yes, I heard that.

580
00:34:25,065 --> 00:34:28,025
Would you put this on the dining room table?
Please be careful with it.

581
00:34:28,110 --> 00:34:29,527
[inhales] Made it myself.

582
00:34:30,571 --> 00:34:31,612
You did?

583
00:34:31,697 --> 00:34:32,656
It's Niobe.

584
00:34:32,739 --> 00:34:34,366
- A Greek queen.
- [Alice gasps softly]

585
00:34:34,449 --> 00:34:36,534
- She's Edgar's favorite.
- [Alice] It's pretty.

586
00:34:37,244 --> 00:34:38,286
Yeah.

587
00:34:39,288 --> 00:34:40,121
Why did you stop?

588
00:34:41,290 --> 00:34:44,293
First, the kids.
Then my sister Bonnie got sick.

589
00:34:44,835 --> 00:34:46,712
[whispers]
And my mother couldn't live on her own.

590
00:34:47,379 --> 00:34:48,172
Well...

591
00:34:49,547 --> 00:34:50,882
You had a gift. It's a shame.

592
00:34:51,592 --> 00:34:52,717
Why is it a shame?

593
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:54,969
I was with the people I love.

594
00:34:56,013 --> 00:34:56,972
Building a life.

595
00:34:58,140 --> 00:35:01,435
You know, without my family, I'm nothing.

596
00:35:04,146 --> 00:35:06,648
[joyful chatter on video]

597
00:35:06,732 --> 00:35:07,608
[cameraman] <i>Testing.</i>

598
00:35:09,860 --> 00:35:11,320
[both laughing]

599
00:35:11,987 --> 00:35:12,779
[chuckles softly]

600
00:35:14,698 --> 00:35:15,616
[Max whimpering]

601
00:35:17,326 --> 00:35:18,785
[chatter continues on video]

602
00:35:26,752 --> 00:35:27,878
[Susan] Thank you, Joseph.

603
00:35:29,046 --> 00:35:30,088
That was beautiful.

604
00:35:30,881 --> 00:35:33,717
[Edgar coughing]

605
00:35:33,800 --> 00:35:34,843
- [Max whimpering]
- [Edgar continues coughing]

606
00:35:34,927 --> 00:35:35,802
You okay?

607
00:35:35,886 --> 00:35:37,054
[Edgar] Mmm.

608
00:35:37,179 --> 00:35:38,430
I'm good.

609
00:35:40,307 --> 00:35:41,099
[Edgar coughs]

610
00:35:45,354 --> 00:35:46,188
No.

611
00:35:47,773 --> 00:35:49,024
That's Will's seat.

612
00:35:49,107 --> 00:35:51,985
[Polly] Oh. My big boy, Will.

613
00:35:52,069 --> 00:35:53,654
When does he get here?

614
00:35:54,363 --> 00:35:55,239
- [table clatters]
- [Max whimpers]

615
00:35:59,243 --> 00:36:00,369
[chair scraping]

616
00:36:04,748 --> 00:36:07,417
Edgar. Would you do the wine, please?

617
00:36:07,501 --> 00:36:08,377
[Edgar] Mmm.

618
00:36:09,211 --> 00:36:10,504
[Edgar grunts softly]

619
00:36:10,629 --> 00:36:12,965
Oh, don't worry. I got it.

620
00:36:14,216 --> 00:36:15,384
[exhales]

621
00:36:17,553 --> 00:36:19,388
[Joseph] Mmm, so good.

622
00:36:20,514 --> 00:36:23,350
They're premade. I just heated them.

623
00:36:23,934 --> 00:36:25,686
Joseph is right, they're... they're delicious.

624
00:36:26,520 --> 00:36:27,938
I would never guess it was frozen.

625
00:36:28,981 --> 00:36:30,399
That's concerning.

626
00:36:32,526 --> 00:36:33,569
Hmm?

627
00:36:33,694 --> 00:36:36,864
It's clearly frozen food on paper plates.

628
00:36:37,573 --> 00:36:40,659
If you manage the restaurant alone,
you'll need to know frozen from fresh.

629
00:36:40,742 --> 00:36:42,286
- [cork pops]
- [Alice] Mmm.

630
00:36:46,707 --> 00:36:47,916
About the restaurant...

631
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,835
I'm-- I'm not sure I plan to...

632
00:36:51,837 --> 00:36:54,089
Let's just talk about it another time.

633
00:36:54,173 --> 00:36:55,716
- Let's talk about it now.
- [soft tense music playing]

634
00:36:56,300 --> 00:36:58,010
- We're all here.
- [Max whimpers]

635
00:36:58,093 --> 00:37:02,639
Well, I haven't decided anything,
but, I mean, it was Will's restaurant--

636
00:37:02,723 --> 00:37:03,807
You ran the place together.

637
00:37:03,891 --> 00:37:05,225
I only did the accounting.

638
00:37:05,309 --> 00:37:07,853
But you're... his wife.

639
00:37:13,859 --> 00:37:14,693
You sure?

640
00:37:18,614 --> 00:37:21,867
[Alice] To be honest, I-- I was thinking,
I might go back to Paris for a while.

641
00:37:23,452 --> 00:37:25,495
Maybe stay with my... with my dad.

642
00:37:26,038 --> 00:37:29,041
Then things seem
a little more decided than you let on.

643
00:37:30,042 --> 00:37:30,834
No, no, no.

644
00:37:30,918 --> 00:37:32,628
These things should be dealt with
as a family.

645
00:37:32,753 --> 00:37:33,587
Yeah.

646
00:37:34,463 --> 00:37:36,882
- We should deal with it as a family.
- [whimpers]

647
00:37:37,007 --> 00:37:39,343
[Susan] You know the staff adores you.

648
00:37:39,426 --> 00:37:41,887
Alice, they need you.

649
00:37:42,888 --> 00:37:45,349
Think about Will. Do it for him.

650
00:37:46,767 --> 00:37:49,061
Wait, I recognize you.

651
00:37:49,728 --> 00:37:52,231
You're married to my grandson, aren't you?

652
00:37:54,399 --> 00:37:56,860
Don't turn a deaf ear.
I asked you a question.

653
00:37:56,944 --> 00:37:57,945
It's all right. [shushes]

654
00:37:58,070 --> 00:37:59,780
- I--
- It's okay. It's okay.

655
00:38:00,489 --> 00:38:02,658
All I'm saying is

656
00:38:03,200 --> 00:38:05,410
you have the chance
to take over a successful business

657
00:38:05,494 --> 00:38:07,663
while honoring Will at the same time.

658
00:38:08,497 --> 00:38:09,998
It was his life's work.

659
00:38:10,082 --> 00:38:11,208
It was his passion.

660
00:38:12,334 --> 00:38:13,752
And you should carry it on.

661
00:38:13,836 --> 00:38:16,797
Susan, I really think
we should do this another time.

662
00:38:16,922 --> 00:38:19,967
No, now's the best time
to lay everything on the table.

663
00:38:20,050 --> 00:38:21,426
- [Susan] He's right.
- [soft tense music continues]

664
00:38:21,510 --> 00:38:23,470
- We need to make decisions together.
- You are driving me fucking crazy!

665
00:38:23,554 --> 00:38:25,848
<i>Without me you are nothing, Alice.</i>

666
00:38:25,973 --> 00:38:27,432
- It's what Will would have wanted.
- [Edgar] <i>That's Will's seat.</i>

667
00:38:27,516 --> 00:38:29,518
- That's your fucking problem!
- [Susan] <i>Do it for him.</i>

668
00:38:29,643 --> 00:38:31,228
[Polly] <i>Will. When does he get here?</i>

669
00:38:31,353 --> 00:38:32,813
We're trying to have a fucking kid!

670
00:38:33,438 --> 00:38:36,441
You do not know what you fucking want!

671
00:38:36,525 --> 00:38:38,986
Say it.
Don't you fucking bait me, Alice.

672
00:38:39,111 --> 00:38:40,404
- [distorted warbling]
- [splashes]

673
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,114
Alice!

674
00:38:42,239 --> 00:38:43,699
Please, calm down.

675
00:38:45,158 --> 00:38:46,285
I am calm.

676
00:38:47,661 --> 00:38:48,954
But you shouldn't speak on Will's behalf.

677
00:38:50,664 --> 00:38:51,915
I'm his mother.

678
00:38:51,999 --> 00:38:54,293
No one knows him better than I do.

679
00:38:54,418 --> 00:38:56,128
[Polly slurping]

680
00:38:56,253 --> 00:38:57,171
[Joseph] Grandma, no.

681
00:38:57,296 --> 00:38:58,547
[stops slurping]

682
00:38:58,672 --> 00:39:00,007
Sorry. Okay, look.

683
00:39:00,132 --> 00:39:03,135
We're all here for him,
but I-- I think Alice is right.

684
00:39:03,260 --> 00:39:05,846
- This isn't the right time to--
- It's never the right time for you, is it?

685
00:39:05,971 --> 00:39:07,306
[uneasy music continues]

686
00:39:09,099 --> 00:39:10,893
That's why you've done nothing
with your life.

687
00:39:11,018 --> 00:39:12,311
Edgar. Please.

688
00:39:12,394 --> 00:39:14,021
- Don't you fucking touch me.
- Edgar,

689
00:39:14,104 --> 00:39:17,024
we're all grieving here,
but that's no reason to be cruel.

690
00:39:17,149 --> 00:39:18,775
- Thya, it's fine.
- It's not.

691
00:39:18,859 --> 00:39:20,485
- Joe...
- Where is it?

692
00:39:20,611 --> 00:39:22,905
[soft tense music playing]

693
00:39:23,030 --> 00:39:24,323
Where's the wedding ring?

694
00:39:25,908 --> 00:39:27,242
Why aren't you wearing it?

695
00:39:27,326 --> 00:39:28,160
Did you sell it?

696
00:39:28,285 --> 00:39:29,328
[Max whimpering]

697
00:39:29,453 --> 00:39:32,122
- You get a good price?
- No! No, no, of course not.

698
00:39:32,206 --> 00:39:34,458
- I...
- Edgar, can I have the corkscrew, please?

699
00:39:35,292 --> 00:39:36,210
[Max whimpering]

700
00:39:36,335 --> 00:39:40,339
[Edgar] And a hoodie and sneakers
at her husband's funeral.

701
00:39:40,464 --> 00:39:42,674
I'm right here, Edgar.
You can speak to me directly.

702
00:39:42,758 --> 00:39:44,092
You didn't even cry.

703
00:39:45,761 --> 00:39:47,763
Don't you think that's weird?

704
00:39:47,888 --> 00:39:48,972
People grieve in different--

705
00:39:49,056 --> 00:39:49,890
- [Edgar] Get away from me!
- [Max squealing]

706
00:39:50,933 --> 00:39:52,601
[Max whimpering]

707
00:40:07,533 --> 00:40:08,492
[coughs]

708
00:40:09,076 --> 00:40:10,744
[huffing]

709
00:40:10,827 --> 00:40:11,787
[Edgar] Will's dead.

710
00:40:12,371 --> 00:40:14,206
And now you inflict this on us?

711
00:40:15,499 --> 00:40:16,667
That's enough.

712
00:40:16,750 --> 00:40:18,085
Dad. You don't look good--

713
00:40:18,210 --> 00:40:19,962
It's your fault he's dead.

714
00:40:20,087 --> 00:40:21,296
[unsettling music playing]

715
00:40:21,380 --> 00:40:23,215
You didn't stop him getting to the car!

716
00:40:23,340 --> 00:40:26,260
Stop it, Dad. I had nothing to do with it.
Will got into a fight with Alice, and he--

717
00:40:26,385 --> 00:40:28,679
What? Are you implying it was my fault?

718
00:40:28,804 --> 00:40:30,347
- No, no, of course not.
- You were there.

719
00:40:30,430 --> 00:40:31,723
You couldn't stop him
from getting in the car either.

720
00:40:31,807 --> 00:40:33,016
[Joseph] I know. Alice, I know, I tried.

721
00:40:33,100 --> 00:40:34,518
- [Alice] We tried. Okay, I didn't.
- [Max whimpers]

722
00:40:34,643 --> 00:40:35,477
- That doesn't mean it's my fault.
- That's not what I'm saying--

723
00:40:35,561 --> 00:40:36,812
- This is exactly what you said.
- [Joseph] Alice, no.

724
00:40:36,937 --> 00:40:38,105
- Alice, I think--
- [Alice] No. I think

725
00:40:38,230 --> 00:40:40,524
you should all mind your own business.
You don't know anything.

726
00:40:40,649 --> 00:40:41,692
[Max whimpering]

727
00:40:41,817 --> 00:40:43,110
You're glad he's dead.

728
00:40:43,235 --> 00:40:46,405
Please, please, please.
Will's looking down on us from above.

729
00:40:48,156 --> 00:40:49,157
From above?

730
00:40:53,537 --> 00:40:56,123
He's down below.

731
00:40:56,248 --> 00:40:57,291
[Max whimpering]

732
00:40:57,416 --> 00:40:58,625
- [grunts]
- [continues whimpering]

733
00:40:58,709 --> 00:41:01,545
- [shouting]
- [Max yelping in pain]

734
00:41:04,590 --> 00:41:05,716
Stop!

735
00:41:06,884 --> 00:41:07,926
[Edgar grunts]

736
00:41:08,010 --> 00:41:09,011
[Joseph] The dog!

737
00:41:09,136 --> 00:41:11,305
- [panting]
- [Edgar] Help me.

738
00:41:11,388 --> 00:41:12,306
[gasping in fright]

739
00:41:12,389 --> 00:41:13,473
Help me.

740
00:41:13,557 --> 00:41:14,641
Help me!

741
00:41:14,725 --> 00:41:15,976
- Get your keys.
- Okay.

742
00:41:17,019 --> 00:41:17,853
[Thya] Let's take him to the hospital!

743
00:41:19,771 --> 00:41:21,190
[Joseph] Thya! I need help! Grab his arm!

744
00:41:21,315 --> 00:41:23,192
[Thya] I got him! I got him!

745
00:41:23,317 --> 00:41:25,152
What did we do to deserve this?

746
00:41:25,277 --> 00:41:26,069
[door slams]

747
00:41:27,321 --> 00:41:29,406
They left without saying goodbye.

748
00:41:30,908 --> 00:41:33,202
[suspenseful music playing]

749
00:41:35,287 --> 00:41:37,456
Jesus fucking Christ, is he fucking crazy?

750
00:41:37,581 --> 00:41:38,665
Thya, please. Give me a second.

751
00:41:38,749 --> 00:41:40,876
- He killed your fucking dog!
- I know!

752
00:41:41,001 --> 00:41:42,419
[Joseph panting]

753
00:41:42,503 --> 00:41:45,172
Shit, shit.
He's fucking bleeding everywhere. Shit.

754
00:41:45,297 --> 00:41:46,548
[panting]

755
00:41:46,632 --> 00:41:48,884
Shit, shit. Come on!

756
00:41:49,593 --> 00:41:51,470
[Joseph breathing heavily]

757
00:41:51,595 --> 00:41:53,847
[foreboding music playing]

758
00:41:53,931 --> 00:41:54,765
[Thya] Joe?

759
00:41:55,349 --> 00:41:56,350
- [Joseph] What?
- Your dad.

760
00:41:58,727 --> 00:42:00,729
[tense music playing]

761
00:42:09,947 --> 00:42:11,156
[yelps]

762
00:42:11,240 --> 00:42:12,950
- No! No!
- [Edgar grunts]

763
00:42:13,033 --> 00:42:13,951
[Joseph] No!

764
00:42:15,035 --> 00:42:16,203
- [grunts]
- [Thya yelps]

765
